WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.306 --> 00:00:03.841
TO MIGRANTS WHO FEARED GANG

00:00:02.507 --> 00:00:04.575
VIOLENCE OR DOMESTIC VIOLENCE IN

00:00:03.975 --> 00:00:07.612
THEIR HOME COUNTRIES.

00:00:04.709 --> 00:00:09.480
IT TURNED OUT THAT THE MAJORITY

00:00:07.745 --> 00:00:11.282
OF THOSE APPLICATIONS WERE

00:00:09.614 --> 00:00:12.150
FALSE.

00:00:11.416 --> 00:00:12.517
MR. ATTORNEY GENERAL JOINS US

00:00:12.283 --> 00:00:14.886
TONIGHT.

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:15.620
SO, I WANT TO ASK YOU THIS.

00:00:15.019 --> 00:00:19.524
BUT FIRST I HAVE TO ASK YOU

00:00:15.753 --> 00:00:20.224
ABOUT A PIECE OF BREAKING NEWS.

00:00:19.657 --> 00:00:23.394
CATHERINE HERRIDGE JUST SAID

00:00:20.358 --> 00:00:24.562
THAT IN JANUARY OF THIS YEAR,

00:00:23.528 --> 00:00:26.064
JANUARY 10, DEPUTY

00:00:24.696 --> 00:00:28.066
GENERAL ROSENSTEIN WENT UP AND

00:00:26.197 --> 00:00:29.300
MET WITH MEMBERS OF THE HOUSE

00:00:28.199 --> 00:00:30.301
INTEL COMMITTEE, HAD A DISPUTE

00:00:29.434 --> 00:00:32.303
WITH THEM AND THREATENED THEM

00:00:30.435 --> 00:00:33.705
WITH A SUBPOENA OF THEIR EMAILS

00:00:32.437 --> 00:00:34.872
AND PHONE RECORDS.

00:00:33.838 --> 00:00:37.709
THIS IS WHAT ONE OF THEM SAID

00:00:35.006 --> 00:00:38.910
IT, I READ IT AS A NOT SO VEILED

00:00:37.842 --> 00:00:40.311
THREAT TO RELEASE FULL

00:00:39.043 --> 00:00:41.512
PROSECUTORIAL POWER OF THE STATE

00:00:40.445 --> 00:00:42.714
AGAINST US.

00:00:41.646 --> 00:00:43.848
THE DOJ BACKGROUND HAS CONFIRMED

00:00:42.847 --> 00:00:45.116
THAT SOMETHING LIKE THIS DID

00:00:43.982 --> 00:00:46.417
HAPPEN.

00:00:45.249 --> 00:00:48.586
WHAT WAS THAT ABOUT?

00:00:46.551 --> 00:00:49.954
&gt;&gt; I DON'T KNOW THAT THEY HAVE

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:53.591
CONFIRMED THAT EXACTLY.

00:00:50.088 --> 00:00:56.294
IN FACT, THE FBI DIRECTOR, THE

00:00:53.725 --> 00:00:58.696
SENIOR EFFECTS COMMITTEE SAY

00:00:56.427 --> 00:01:00.298
THAT IS A MISCHARACTERIZATION,

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:02.500
REALLY, OF WHAT OCCURRED.

00:01:00.431 --> 00:01:04.502
ALSO, I THINK IT INDICATES THAT

00:01:02.633 --> 00:01:07.372
THERE HAS BEEN A BREAKDOWN OF

00:01:04.635 --> 00:01:09.474
RELATIONSHIPS, WHEN IN FACT,

00:01:07.505 --> 00:01:11.175
SINCE JANUARY, A GREAT DEAL OF

00:01:09.607 --> 00:01:12.110
PROGRESS HAS BEEN MADE.

00:01:11.309 --> 00:01:18.116
WE UNDERSTAND IN THIS DEPARTMENT

00:01:12.243 --> 00:01:19.283
THAT WE ARE ACCOUNTABLE TO

00:01:18.249 --> 00:01:20.885
CONGRESS AND WE NEED TO BE

00:01:19.417 --> 00:01:22.553
COOPERATIVE WITH THEM, TO

00:01:21.019 --> 00:01:24.889
PRODUCE AS MANY DOCUMENTS AS

00:01:22.687 --> 00:01:28.893
RATIONALLY, LEGALLY AND PROPERLY

00:01:25.023 --> 00:01:29.660
AS CAN BE PRODUCING THEM, AND WE

00:01:29.027 --> 00:01:35.266
HAVE MADE DRAMATIC PROGRESS IN

00:01:29.794 --> 00:01:35.900
THAT REGARD REALLY.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:36.667
&gt;&gt; Tucker: DID THE DEPUTY

00:01:36.034 --> 00:01:38.102
ATTORNEY GENERAL THREATENED TO A

00:01:36.801 --> 00:01:40.872
SUBPOENA ON THE EMAIL OR PHONE

00:01:38.236 --> 00:01:41.372
RECORDS OF MEMBERS OF THE HOUSE

00:01:41.005 --> 00:01:43.107
INTEL COMMITTEE?

00:01:41.506 --> 00:01:44.876
I WAS NOT IN THE ROOM AND I

00:01:43.241 --> 00:01:47.512
CANNOT SPEAK TO WHAT OCCURRED.

00:01:45.009 --> 00:01:49.280
ALL I CAN SAY IS THAT THE

00:01:47.845 --> 00:01:50.248
PEOPLE -- THE DIRECTOR OF THE

00:01:49.414 --> 00:01:52.717
FBI AT OUR SENIOR ETHICS

00:01:50.381 --> 00:01:55.787
ATTORNEY WAS THERE AND OTHERS

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:56.220
AND THEY DID NOT SEE THAT IN THE

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.289
SAME FASHION.

00:01:56.354 --> 00:02:01.059
&gt;&gt; Tucker: SO AS A FACTUAL

00:01:58.423 --> 00:02:01.692
MATTER, YOU DON'T THINK THAT

00:02:01.192 --> 00:02:04.495
HAPPENED?

00:02:01.826 --> 00:02:05.863
&gt;&gt; I'M CONFIDENT THAT DEPUTY

00:02:04.629 --> 00:02:08.332
ROSENSTEIN AFTER 28 YEARS AND

00:02:05.997 --> 00:02:09.067
THE DEPARTMENT OF JUSTICE DID

00:02:08.466 --> 00:02:11.269
NOT IMPROPERLY THREATEN ANYONE

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:13.371
ON THAT OCCASION.

00:02:11.402 --> 00:02:16.107
BUT WE DO BELIEVE THAT WE HAVE

00:02:13.504 --> 00:02:17.608
TRIED TO BE COOPERATIVE WITH

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:21.479
THEM AND MADE PROGRESS IN

00:02:17.742 --> 00:02:21.746
MONTHS, AS THE MONTHS HAVE GONE

00:02:21.612 --> 00:02:23.848
BY.

00:02:21.879 --> 00:02:25.583
IN FACT, WE HAVE HAD SOME GOOD

00:02:23.981 --> 00:02:26.684
RELATIONSHIPS WITH THE MEMBERS

00:02:25.716 --> 00:02:27.285
OF CONGRESS.

00:02:26.818 --> 00:02:28.286
IT'S.

00:02:27.418 --> 00:02:30.621
&gt;&gt; Tucker: OKAY.

00:02:28.419 --> 00:02:31.923
SO YOU HAVE MADE NEWS RECENTLY

00:02:30.755 --> 00:02:35.493
BY UNDOING AN OBAMA ERA RULE

00:02:32.056 --> 00:02:36.894
ABOUT ASYLUM-SEEKERS.

00:02:35.626 --> 00:02:37.829
GIVE US THE OVERVIEW.

00:02:37.028 --> 00:02:39.564
I THINK MOST AMERICANS LIKE THE

00:02:37.962 --> 00:02:40.731
IDEA THAT THIS CAN BE A HAVEN

00:02:39.697 --> 00:02:41.732
FOR PEOPLE SUFFERING AROUND THE

00:02:40.865 --> 00:02:43.067
WORLD.

00:02:41.866 --> 00:02:44.469
LOTS OF PEOPLE CLAIM ASYLUM,

00:02:43.201 --> 00:02:47.905
WHAT DO WE KNOW ABOUT THE

00:02:44.602 --> 00:02:50.508
VERACITY OF THEIR CLAIMS?

00:02:48.039 --> 00:02:53.678
&gt;&gt; THAT'S A GOOD QUESTION.

00:02:50.641 --> 00:02:55.613
SEVEN YEARS AGO, 5,000 PEOPLE

00:02:53.811 --> 00:02:57.181
APPLIED FOR ASYLUM CLAIMING A

00:02:55.746 --> 00:02:59.917
CREDIBLE FEAR OF BEING AT HOME

00:02:57.315 --> 00:03:01.919
IN THEIR HOME COUNTRY, AND THEY

00:03:00.051 --> 00:03:06.324
NEEDED TO FLEE THAT COUNTRY.

00:03:02.053 --> 00:03:07.125
THAT NUMBER JUMPED TO 94,000 IN

00:03:06.457 --> 00:03:09.694
JUST SEVEN YEARS.

00:03:07.258 --> 00:03:11.496
IT IS OVERWHELMING OUR SYSTEM.

00:03:09.827 --> 00:03:14.298
OVER 80% OF THOSE CLAIMS ARE

00:03:11.629 --> 00:03:15.900
BEING DENIED BY THE IMMIGRATION

00:03:14.432 --> 00:03:19.070
JUDGES AS BEING NOT MERITORIOUS.

00:03:16.033 --> 00:03:19.804
SO IT IS A BIG PROBLEM FOR US.

00:03:19.203 --> 00:03:22.507
EACH ONE OF THOSE IS REQUIRING

00:03:19.937 --> 00:03:23.641
TRIALS AND FACTUAL DECISIONS BY

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:26.911
OUR JUDGES.

00:03:23.774 --> 00:03:30.081
WE ARE GOING TO ADD 100 JUDGES,

00:03:27.044 --> 00:03:31.282
AND THAT MAY YET NOT BE ENOUGH

00:03:30.214 --> 00:03:34.452
JUDGES TO HANDLE THE CASES.

00:03:31.415 --> 00:03:38.689
WE NEED TO GET THE JUDGE IS

00:03:34.585 --> 00:03:41.092
BETTER GUIDANCE, GO BACK TO THE

00:03:38.823 --> 00:03:42.093
FUNDAMENTAL PRINCIPLES, LAWS AND

00:03:41.225 --> 00:03:42.627
RULES OF THE IMMIGRATION AND

00:03:42.226 --> 00:03:44.529
NATIONALIZATION ACT.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:46.097
IF WE DO THAT, THEN WE ARE IN A

00:03:44.662 --> 00:03:48.099
POSITION WHERE SOME OF THESE

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:49.534
CASES CAN BE PROMPTLY DECIDED.

00:03:48.232 --> 00:03:56.974
WE DO NOT GET TO COME TO AMERICA

00:03:49.667 --> 00:03:58.109
IF YOU HAVE A PRIVATE THREAT OR

00:03:57.108 --> 00:04:00.011
SOMEONE PERSONALLY ATTACKS YOU.

00:03:58.242 --> 00:04:01.879
YOU DO NOT GET TO HAVE ASYLUM

00:04:00.144 --> 00:04:04.448
FOR THAT, BASED ON YOUR RACE,

00:04:02.013 --> 00:04:06.284
RELIGION OR NATIONALITY, THAT

00:04:04.582 --> 00:04:07.818
YOU ARE PART OF SOME SPECIAL

00:04:06.417 --> 00:04:10.855
IDENTIFIABLE GROUP THAT HAS BEEN

00:04:07.952 --> 00:04:14.025
PERSECUTED IN YOUR HOME COUNTRY.

00:04:10.988 --> 00:04:15.860
THAT'S WHAT IT TAKES TO HAVE

00:04:14.158 --> 00:04:16.494
ASYLUM AND I THINK IT WILL HELP

00:04:15.993 --> 00:04:19.030
US.

00:04:16.627 --> 00:04:20.932
AT THE DECISION I MADE, I

00:04:19.163 --> 00:04:22.099
BELIEVE IT'S RIGHT LEGALLY AND

00:04:21.065 --> 00:04:24.101
I'M TOTALLY CONFIDENT IT'S

00:04:22.233 --> 00:04:26.370
CONSISTENT WITH THE INTENT OF

00:04:24.235 --> 00:04:26.904
THE DRAFTERS OF THE INA, OUR

00:04:26.504 --> 00:04:29.140
LAW.

00:04:27.038 --> 00:04:29.874
I BELIEVE IT WILL HELP US MANAGE

00:04:29.273 --> 00:04:31.809
OUR CASELOADS BETTER AND GIVE

00:04:30.007 --> 00:04:35.112
MORE FOCUS TO THE PEOPLE WHO

00:04:31.943 --> 00:04:37.315
DESERVE TO BE GIVEN ASYLUM AND

00:04:35.246 --> 00:04:38.349
HELP US ELIMINATE THOSE WHO ARE

00:04:37.448 --> 00:04:40.785
NOT WORTHY OF THE ASYLUM.

00:04:38.482 --> 00:04:42.787
&gt;&gt; Tucker: WITH OVER 80% OF

00:04:40.918 --> 00:04:46.290
THE APPLICATIONS ARE FRAUDULENT,

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:46.991
THERE'S OBVIOUSLY A PROBLEM.

00:04:46.424 --> 00:04:49.860
SO THEY HAVE ALSO RECENTLY

00:04:47.124 --> 00:04:51.295
WEIGHED IN WITH THE QUESTION OF

00:04:49.994 --> 00:04:51.963
SPEECH ON CAMPUS.

00:04:51.429 --> 00:04:52.997
WHAT CAN THE DEPARTMENT OF

00:04:52.096 --> 00:04:55.266
JUSTICE DO TO ENSURE THAT

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:55.733
PEOPLE'S FIRST AMENDMENT RIGHTS

00:04:55.399 --> 00:04:59.370
ARE PROTECTED?

00:04:55.866 --> 00:05:01.105
AND WHY HAS IT TAKEN UNTIL 2018

00:04:59.503 --> 00:05:02.340
TO GET THE DOJ INVOLVED?

00:05:01.239 --> 00:05:03.808
&gt;&gt; IT'S ONE OF THE BIG

00:05:02.473 --> 00:05:06.110
CHALLENGES OF OUR TIME, I HAVE

00:05:03.941 --> 00:05:08.145
COME TO BELIEVE, AND IT'S ALMOST

00:05:06.244 --> 00:05:09.914
UNBELIEVABLE THAT MAJOR COLLEGES

00:05:08.279 --> 00:05:10.915
AND UNIVERSITIES WILL BE TAKEN

00:05:10.047 --> 00:05:14.051
ACTION THAT RESTRICTS THE RIGHT

00:05:11.048 --> 00:05:16.487
OF FREE SPEECH ON A COLLEGE

00:05:14.185 --> 00:05:18.055
CAMPUS.

00:05:16.621 --> 00:05:22.493
WE HAVE THE AUTHORITY ON THE LAW

00:05:18.189 --> 00:05:23.494
TO FILE A STATEMENT OF INTEREST

00:05:22.627 --> 00:05:25.162
IN ONGOING LITIGATION.

00:05:23.628 --> 00:05:26.998
SO CASES ARE BEING FILED AGAINST

00:05:25.296 --> 00:05:27.365
THE UNIVERSITIES BY STUDENTS WHO

00:05:27.131 --> 00:05:30.901
COMPLAIN.

00:05:27.498 --> 00:05:33.704
IF WE THINK THE COMPLAINTS ARE

00:05:31.035 --> 00:05:34.672
MERITORIOUS, THEN WE CAN FILE A

00:05:33.838 --> 00:05:39.310
STATEMENT OF INTEREST JOINING

00:05:34.805 --> 00:05:40.544
WITH THEM, AND EXPLAIN WHY WE AT

00:05:39.443 --> 00:05:45.149
THE DEPARTMENT OF JUSTICE THINK

00:05:40.678 --> 00:05:55.293
THESE CONCERNS ARE REAL AND

00:05:45.283 --> 00:05:55.693
JUSTIFIED, AND COURT RELIEF IS

00:05:55.426 --> 00:05:56.327
APPROPRIATE.

00:05:55.826 --> 00:05:56.994
WE HAVE HAD SOME SUCCESS.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:57.728
WE HAVE HAD TWO CASES WHERE

00:05:57.128 --> 00:05:58.396
THERE HAS BEEN A MAJOR CHANGE IN

00:05:57.862 --> 00:05:59.130
THE COLLEGE AND UNIVERSITY'S

00:05:58.529 --> 00:05:59.864
ACTIONS, AND TWO CASES WHERE THE

00:05:59.263 --> 00:06:01.232
JUDGE HAS DISMISSED OR REJECTED

00:05:59.997 --> 00:06:04.135
A MOTION TO DISMISS THESE CASES

00:06:01.365 --> 00:06:05.670
BY THE UNIVERSITIES, AND

00:06:04.268 --> 00:06:06.103
ALLOWING THE TRIAL TO GO

00:06:05.803 --> 00:06:09.240
FORWARD.

00:06:06.237 --> 00:06:11.275
WE THINK IT IS A VERY IMPORTANT

00:06:09.373 --> 00:06:12.710
THING.

00:06:11.409 --> 00:06:15.713
STUDENTS SHOULD BE PARTICIPATING

00:06:12.843 --> 00:06:16.781
IN ROBUST DEBATE, THEY OUGHT TO

00:06:15.846 --> 00:06:19.083
NOT BE INTIMIDATED, THEY OUGHT

00:06:16.914 --> 00:06:20.751
TO NOT BE DRIVEN BY POLITICAL

00:06:19.216 --> 00:06:24.121
CORRECTNESS, TO WHERE YOU CAN'T

00:06:20.885 --> 00:06:26.657
EVEN SPEAK UP IN CLASS OR ON

00:06:24.255 --> 00:06:29.660
CAMPUS.

